      "where": "/museum/network-onchain and /museum/network-onchain/texts · default · 390x844",
      "evidence": "evidence/index-390x844-02.png",
      "observation": "Resolved. Index text and tiles at 390 px show a 'Back to the sections' link at the end of every work and section group (index-390x844-03.png, text/index-390x844.txt), so one tap from the bottom of any section reaches the chip row. The texts page is a single filtered list with no section chips, so no return path is needed there.",
      "consequence": "A reader at the bottom of the index, such as the verification block or the releases, must scroll the whole page to reach another section.",
      "change": "Add a 'Back to sections' link (href to the chip row) at the end of each section, or make the chip row sticky below the site header.",
      "acceptance_check": "From the bottom of the index at 390 px, one tap returns to the section list or reaches any section.",
      "admission": "baseline",
      "reopen_reason": null
    },
    {
      "id": "V-005",
      "targets": [
        "J03",
        "J10"
      ],
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "resolved",
      "where": "/museum/network-onchain/records/* · default · 1440x1000",
      "evidence": "evidence/record-work-1440x1000-01.png",
      "observation": "Resolved. At 1440 px the work image and the credit, licence and rights link now share the first screen in two columns (record-work-1440x1000-01.png, record-work-portrait-1440x1000-01.png); at 820 px and 390 px the stack is unchanged (record-work-820x1000-01.png). The caption sits far right with a wide gutter on the portrait work; this is a taste point, not a defect.",
      "consequence": "On desktop the art gets no more presence than on a tablet, and the caption and facts are a full screen below it.",
      "change": "At 1440 px put the image and the title, credit and licence lines side by side in one row, with the image in the larger column; keep the stack below 1024 px.",
      "acceptance_check": "At 1440 px the work image and its caption or key fields share the first screen; at 820 and 390 px the stack is unchanged.",
      "admission": "baseline",
      "reopen_reason": null
    },
    {
      "id": "V-001",
      "targets": [
        "J05",
        "J03"
      ],
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "resolved",
      "where": "/museum/network-onchain · default · 1440x1000 and 820x1000",
      "evidence": "evidence/index-1440x1000-02.png",
      "observation": "Resolved. The work grids now flow in columns (masonry): images sit directly under the caption above, with no blank band between cells at 1440 or 820 px. Only the natural ragged ends of the columns remain.",
      "consequence": "The grid reads as uneven and unfinished, and the eye cannot scan the works in order. Blank bands break the pacing of a page whose subject is the art.",
      "change": "Lay the works out in rows that share a height (justified rows with each image at its own aspect ratio), or fill columns top to bottom, so no cell leaves an empty band under shorter neighbours.",
      "acceptance_check": "At 1440, 820 and 390 px no grid row leaves a vertical gap larger than the caption height between an image block and the next row; every image keeps its aspect ratio.",
      "admission": "baseline",
      "reopen_reason": null
    },
    {
      "id": "V-003",
      "targets": [
        "J03",
        "J05"
      ],
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "resolved",
      "where": "All record routes · default · 1440x1000, 820x1000, 390x844",
      "evidence": "evidence/record-rights-390x844-02.png",
